    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "Nigerian hyperrealist artist based in Lagos, born 1993; self-taught, studied architecture at Federal Polytechnic Nekede. Uses blue Bic ballpoint pen exclusively since 2014 for large-scale photorealistic portraits (200-400 hours per piece). Fully autonomous independent practice: sells work via his own store, gallery representation at Omenka Gallery (Lagos) and Voltz Clarke Gallery (New York); placed 6th in BIC Art Master 2020. Explores Afrorealism and Black identity. Established artist, senior/mid-career level; Autonomy 5 (fully self-directed, sets his own vision, no employer). Work Status Freelance: site and store indicate independent commission/sales practice; no employed role found. Country corrected from Kenya (migration error) to Nigeria (confirmed Wikipedia, ItsNiceThat, own site). LinkedIn snippet lists Creative Director (likely self-applied title for his own practice).",
